\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  From Thee all skill and science flow,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 All pity, care, and love,
\par All calm and courage, faith and hope;
\par O pour them from above.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. And part them, Lord, to each and all,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 As each and all shall need,
\par To rise like incense, each to Thee,
\par In noble thought and deed.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  And hasten, Lord, that perfect day
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 When pain and death shall cease,
\par And Thy just rule shall fill the earth
\par with health, and light, and peace:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  When ever blue the sky shall gleam,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 And ever green the sod;
\par And man's rude work deface no more
\par \pard    The Paradise of God.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

